cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "pypfda: Particle filter data assimilation in pure Python"
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the methodological paper below."
type: software
# The accompanying paper pins v1.0 (`pip install "pypfda[plot]==1.0"`), and v1.0 is the
# archived version of record on Zenodo, so this file cites v1.0. v1.1.0 (2026-07-28) adds a
# transient-forcing calendar, SST archiving and two Lorenz-63 examples; it reproduces every
# v1.0 result exactly and is tagged as `v1.1.0` if you need it.
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-06-10"
authors:
  - given-names: Bijan
    family-names: Fallah
    email: bijan.fallah@gmail.com
    affiliation: Potsdam Institute for Climate Impact Research (PIK)
repository-code: "https://github.com/bijanf/pypfda"
url: "https://bijanf.github.io/pypfda"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - data assimilation
  - particle filter
  - sequential Monte Carlo
  - paleoclimate
  - AMOC
  - climate
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "pypfda v1.0: An open-source, model-agnostic particle-filter engine for online sequential paleo data assimilation in Earth system models"
